
Element Operatprs in mongoDB:
---------------------------------------- >

db.collection_name.find( { field:"value " } );

$ exists : Matches documenst that have the specified field.
{field :{ $exists :  <boolean > } }
                              True 
                              False
.> simply here i need all the data where from the collections / rows where age filed exists 

EX-1 : db.MySkills.find({age:{$exists:true}});
EX-2 : db.MySkills.find({age:{$exists:false}})


$ type  : Select  documents if a field is of the specified type.
{ field : { $type: < type > } }
                           dataType.
.> simple here i need all the data where from the rows if the age type is integer.

EX-1: db.MySkills.find({name:{$type:"strin;g" }}) ;
EX-2 : db.MySkills.find({age:{$type:"int"}})  ;

To check for the multiple data types for the particukar filedds we use here array :
EX-3:  db.MySkills.find({age:{$type:["int","string"]}});

The data types which we can pass here in this case:
String
Double
32-bit-Integer
64-bit-Integer
Boolean
Array
Object 
Null
Regular Expression
TimeStamp
Date
ObjectId


